models.description:
User-generated comments attached to articles for community discussion.

Comments enable readers to engage with article content through single-level feedback. Each comment is authored by a registered member and attached to a specific article. Members retain full control over their comments, including editing and deletion rights.

Key relationships:
- Authored by a member: {@link discussion_board_members}
- Attached to an article: {@link discussion_board_articles}

Comments are displayed in chronological order (oldest first) and support full-text search capabilities.

Point-in-time snapshots of comment modifications for audit trail and revision history. Each time a comment is created or modified, a snapshot is captured preserving the exact state at that moment including all field values and foreign key references. This enables version control, content moderation audits, and historical content recovery.

The snapshot denormalizes all parent comment fields to preserve the exact state at snapshot time, even if the parent comment's relationships change later. This is essential for accurate audit trails and historical queries.

Key relationships:
- Belongs to {@link discussion_board_comments} via foreign key
- Denormalizes article reference from {@link discussion_board_articles}
- Denormalizes member reference from {@link discussion_board_members}
